## Highlights
- One of my very favorite lines about being a parent comes from Andrew Solomon’s [*Far From The Tree*](https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0743236726/wwwaustinkleo-20/ref=nosim/): **“Perhaps the immutable error of parenthood is that we give our children what we wanted, whether they want it or not.”** ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01j1fwq3wjn299h05mtk9yrh87))
- Carl Jung said that nothing had a bigger influence on the child than the unlived life of the parent. Those unlived lives linger. ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01j1fwqccyg0w1mkhf82f8ghg3))
- One must be careful to not transfer unwanted dreams onto their children, maybe even more so when your children are inclined to doing the things you, too, love. (One of my sons loves music and video games, the other loves stories and drawing. You can imagine the dreams I have for them, dreams that I find it best to keep to myself.) ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01j1fwqvzbngxagwbr8616jsgj))


